  "description": {
   "content": [
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "This is the AuthFilterJAAS entry from web.xml",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "<filter>",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "<filter-name>AuthFilterJAAS</filter-name>",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "<filter-class>org.fcrepo.server.jaas.AuthFilterJAAS</filter-class>",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "<init-param>",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "<description>OPTIONAL. A comma separated list of class names for user principals. ",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "First one that is found is effective only.</description>",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "<param-name>userClassNames</param-name>",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "<param-value>org.fcrepo.server.jaas.auth.UserPrincipal</param-value>",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "</init-param>",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "<init-param>",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "<description>OPTIONAL. A comma separated list of url-patterns to ignore</description>",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "<param-name>excludeUris</param-name>",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "<param-value>/getDS</param-value>",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "</init-param>",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "</filter>",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "For some reason, the filter does not read the context param",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "<context-param>",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "<param-name>fedora.home</param-name>",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "<param-value>/home/abr/Servers/fcrepo3.3-1</param-value>",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "</context-param>",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "But instead crashes when FEDORA_HOME is not set. The rest of the system works from the context param, so this is somewhat surprising.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "One of the trumped features of Fedora 3.3 was the ability to deploy several servlets. If we still depend on the environment variable, and not the context param, this feature is lost. For that reason, this bug has been marked as major.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    }
   ],
   "type": "doc",
   "version": 1
  },
